# WRITING_ARCHITECT

A governed **Book Production Operating System** — the executable answer to the
forensic specification's verdict: *stop making master prompts; build a stateful,
testable system where the rules are enforced by software.*

- **WR-00 forensics** — read-only recursive fingerprinting, duplicate analysis,
  authority proposal, capability map, and disposition of an archive.
- **WR-01 foundation** — the canonical data model, the B0–B13 lifecycle with
  hard gates, a policy engine, and a tamper-evident audit ledger.

**Zero third-party dependencies. Offline. Stdlib-only Python 3.9+.**

## Quick start

```bash
# 1. install
bash install.sh                 # macOS/Linux   (Windows: install.ps1)

# 2. audit your archive (read-only)
wa forensics WRITING_ARCHITECT.zip --out wr00_baseline
#    -> open wr00_baseline/WR00_REPORT.md

# 3. watch the governance rules enforce themselves
wa demo demo.sqlite

# 4. start a governed book
wa init mybook.sqlite
wa book-new mybook.sqlite --title "Ash and Silence" --author "Brian Fochtman" \
    --audience "Adult literary readers" \
    --reader-promise "A grief-soaked account of exile and return"
wa status mybook.sqlite <book_id>
```

## What to read

| Document | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `docs/GUIDE.md` | Plain-language, start-to-finish operator guide |
| `DIRECTIVE.md` | The governing build directive + live forensic audit findings |
| `wr00_baseline/WR00_REPORT.md` | Generated forensic report on your archive |

## Verify it yourself

```bash
python3 tests/test_system.py      # 12 governance/forensics tests, expect 12 passed
wa doctor                         # installation self-check
```

## Layout

```
writing_architect/
  forensics/    inventory, duplicates, authority, capability_map, baseline  (WR-00)
  domain/       schema.sql, db, lifecycle, policy                           (WR-01)
  cli.py        the `wa` command
  demo.py       spec 14.1 first vertical slice
tests/          test_system.py
docs/GUIDE.md   plain-language guide
DIRECTIVE.md    build directive + audit
install.sh / install.ps1
```

## The rules that are always on (spec 11.3)

1. No draft without an approved chapter contract.
2. No factual claim accepted without supporting evidence.
3. No quotation without an exact location reference.
4. No reviewer closes their own blocker.
5. No overwrite of a released artifact.
6. No lifecycle move without a named actor and a recorded reason.
7. Audit log is append-only and hash-chained.
8. No canonical authority without a supersession rationale.

Enforced by the database and policy engine — not by a prompt.
